&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note what is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; there: no &lt;code&gt;YoSQL&lt;/code&gt; dependency. The plugin runs during the build and the code it
leaves behind needs only the JDK and your driver.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Upgrading</title><link>https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/installation/upgrading/</link><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://yosql.projects.metio.wtf/installation/upgrading/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;What each release needs from you, when it needs anything. Releases not listed here are drop-in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="202698"&gt;2026.9.8&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="converters-are-generated-beside-your-repositories"&gt;Converters are generated beside your repositories&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;converter.mapConverterClass&lt;/code&gt; used to default to &lt;code&gt;com.example.persistence.converter.ToMapConverter&lt;/code&gt;,
and every generated converter is written to the package that setting names. A project that set
&lt;code&gt;repositories.basePackageName&lt;/code&gt; and nothing else therefore had its repositories generated where it
asked and its converters generated into the example&amp;rsquo;s package — a name it had never written down,
reached through a setting it had never heard of.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>